# Supply-chain hardening — disable lifecycle scripts globally.
# Triggered by PostHog Shai-Hulud 2.0 (2025-11-24): trojaned posthog-js@1.297.3 used a malicious
# `preinstall` script to exfiltrate CI/dev/prod secrets via TruffleHog.
# See https://posthog.com/blog/nov-24-shai-hulud-attack-post-mortem
# Allowlist below intentionally empty — add packages here ONLY when their build genuinely needs a
# postinstall AND you have audited what that script does. Re-run `pnpm install` after editing.
ignore-scripts=true
# Allowlisted lifecycle scripts (none at MVP):
# @example/pkg-with-required-build
node-linker=hoisted
